WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.920
Ross and I recently got the privilege

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.350
to meet a remarkable and incredible group of women.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.370
It's as, you know, amazing as it gets.

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.150
They just made history as the first women ever

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.069
to be in the pit crew at the Daytona 500.

6
00:00:16.069 --> 00:00:17.451
(audience cheering wildly)

7
00:00:17.451 --> 00:00:18.451
Take a look.

8
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.860
Please welcome Breanna O'Leary, Bree Daniels,

9
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.950
and Dalanda Ouendeno.

10
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.544
Hi.
(audience clapping)

11
00:00:27.544 --> 00:00:28.461
Hi.
Hey.

12
00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:33.160
Hi.

13
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:35.573
Hello, hello.

14
00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:38.030
Hey, what's going on?

15
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.240
Oh my gosh, we're so excited to meet you.

16
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.090
Bree, you broke a barrier.

17
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.300
You are the first black woman to change tires in NASCAR.

18
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.940
Is that true?

19
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.540
Yes, ma'am.

20
00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.623
Wow.
(audience clapping)

21
00:00:50.623 --> 00:00:51.706
Yes.

22
00:00:53.977 --> 00:00:56.160
How fast can you do it?

23
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.850
And how did you get so good at it?

24
00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.680
I would say I'm pretty fast.

25
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.820 line:15%
One tire is coming off in less than a second,

26
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.710 line:15%
if not, you know, a second at the most,

27
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:08.160 line:15%
and a whole pitstop is done

28
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.770 line:15%
between like 11 and 13 seconds max.

29
00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.290
Whoa. So cool.

30
00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:14.060
And Breanna with Bree, you guys,

31
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.520
you both made history as the first female duo

32
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.810
to ever pit in the Daytona 500, isn't that right?

33
00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:20.840
Yeah, that was us.

34
00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.943
That's amazing. Look at that.

35
00:01:22.943 --> 00:01:23.967
(audience cheering)

36
00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:24.800
A duo.

37
00:01:28.036 --> 00:01:29.960
How does it feel?

38
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.420
It was really empowering, just because me and Brehanna

39
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.960 line:15%
came into the program together.

40
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.410 line:15%
Essentially from day one, me and her were together,

41
00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.570
learning everything.

42
00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.250
So to see the fruits of our labor in such a big stage

43
00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.310
of the Daytona 500, was just so empowering

44
00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.890
and so much fun and we just couldn't believe it.

45
00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.760
And so we just tried to enjoy it the best we could.

46
00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.840
Now, Dalanda, you were a soccer champion,

47
00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.410
and now the first woman from outside of the US to pit,

48
00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.080
is that true?

49
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.940
Yes, yes. That's true.

50
00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.773
Well-

51
00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:08.110
I played the soccer-
(audience cheering)

52
00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.060
Where were you playing soccer?

53
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.190 line:15%
Paris St. Germaine in France for PSG,

54
00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.680 line:15%
and then I got recruited to play D1 in the US

55
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.830 line:15%
for the University of Miami.

56
00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.200 line:15%
I mean, can I ask each and every one of you,

57
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.980 line:15%
why you got into what you got into

58
00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.600 line:15%
and what makes you happy about it?

59
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.310 line:15%
Bree, why did you get into this,

60
00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.000 line:15%
and what does it feed you?

61
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.290
To be honest, I was playing basketball

62
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.090
at Norfolk State University,

63
00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.510
and I've learned that, once I joined the sport,

64
00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.140
not too many of us are doing it, not too many women.

65
00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.220
And, I'm just saying that somebody has to set the tone,

66
00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.530
to be that example for other women

67
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.360
to want to be able to join a sport,

68
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.790
with barely any women in there.

69
00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.380
So, yeah.

70
00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.530
Cool.
Thanks to you.

71
00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.550
You are changing that.
(audience clapping)

72
00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.568
Love that.

73
00:02:59.568 --> 00:03:01.980
Breanna, why did you get into this

74
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.810
and what does it feed you?

75
00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.190
This opportunity from the Drive for Diversity program

76
00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.080
happened to come by my university.

77
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.630
And it was, it was kind of like a why not?

78
00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.410
It wasn't, I didn't know what I was getting myself into

79
00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.580
but I just thought why not?

80
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.100
And it turns out in the whole, grand scheme of things

81
00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.400
probably the most rewarding part of all of it

82
00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.030
is getting to hear that I'm an inspiration

83
00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.730
or that little girls now know

84
00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.070
that they can go change tires if they want to.

85
00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.710
And so that's definitely been the coolest part

86
00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:36.543
of all of this.

87
00:03:36.543 --> 00:03:38.330
I look at that picture of you in the crowd

88
00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.985
on the rail, just soaking it in.

89
00:03:39.985 --> 00:03:41.330
(audience clapping)

90
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.163
Yeah.

91
00:03:42.163 --> 00:03:45.050
And Dalanda, why did you decide to do this?

92
00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.483
And how does it feed you?

93
00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.340
I just wanted to have fun.

94
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.660
I joined NASCAR just to see what was around.

95
00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.080
It was a new experience.

96
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.780
I was like, why not?

97
00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.850
And just going to bed at night,

98
00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:01.786
knowing that you're badass, is just so gratifying.

99
00:04:01.786 --> 00:04:02.619
(audience cheering)

100
00:04:02.619 --> 00:04:03.800
Yes. It does.
Yes, yes.

101
00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.564
Yes it does, and you all are.

102
00:04:06.564 --> 00:04:07.397
That is the best.

103
00:04:07.397 --> 00:04:10.570
And I'm so grateful that you would come here

104
00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:14.440
and tell your stories, and we can see you and hear you

105
00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.250
and celebrate you as we do.

106
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.099
Thank you so much.

107
00:04:19.099 --> 00:04:21.682
(upbeat music)

